// Stepping onto the barrier in the ford while the riders hold it.
@speaker A rider at the barrier
=== start
[flag ford_fought] -> empty
[flag ford_waded] -> waved
A rider wades into the water in front of the stakes, spear held low and easy. "Toll," he says in bad Gaulish. "Five." He holds up five fingers in case you missed it.
* [silver 5] Pay him five silver and wade across. -> paid ~ silver -5
* "I'll talk to Haldo first." -> back
* Push past him. -> fight

=== paid
~ set ford_waded
He steps aside. "Come back soon," he says, and seems pleased with the phrase.
* Cross. -> END

=== waved
The rider looks at you, remembers the five silver, and waves you through with his spear. "Paid. Go."
* Cross. -> END

=== back
He shrugs and points up the bank, toward the fire.
* Go back. -> END ~ travel oltis_ford north

=== fight
~ set ford_fought; fight_all riders
He shouts, and up on the bank everyone is moving.
* Fight. -> END

=== empty
~ set ford_open
Nobody stands at the barrier now. The stakes lean in the current, already half pulled out.
* Cross. -> END
